From c897bf76c506c92dd807a6d993ae2cd0701a555e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:37:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Relink the release list oldest block first

release_unused_nodes read the release list blocks into a queue with the
oldest at the front, then walked it from the back (newest first) while
carrying the new address of each block into the prev pointer of the next
one. That links an older block to the newer one, and leaves the newer
block pointing at the old copy of the older block, which has just been
deallocated. With more than one release list block (more than about 1000
files removed while still open) the files in the other blocks were never
freed, and once the freed block was used again the list could loop, so
the walk never ended.

Walk from the front (oldest first), and write a block again whenever its
prev pointer changed. Writing and removing 3000 files that are still
open, then closing them, now frees all their space (before: about 24 MB
of 36 MB stayed allocated per round).
---
 src/transaction.rs | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/transaction.rs b/src/transaction.rs
index 0ce0fe0..0a969ca 100644
--- a/src/transaction.rs
+++ b/src/transaction.rs
@@ -1262,15 +1262,17 @@ impl<'a, D: Disk> Transaction<'a, D> {
             }
         }
 
-        // Find unused nodes and remove them (going backwards through list)
+        // Find unused nodes and remove them, oldest block first, so that a
+        // block that moves or goes away can be relinked in the next newer one
         let mut update_prev = None;
         let mut release_nodes = Vec::new();
-        while let Some(mut release) = releases.pop_back() {
+        while let Some(mut release) = releases.pop_front() {
+            let mut changed = false;
             if let Some(prev_ptr) = update_prev.take() {
                 release.data_mut().prev = prev_ptr;
+                changed = true;
             }
 
-            let mut changed = false;
             let mut empty = true;
             for entry in release.data_mut().entries.iter_mut() {
                 if !entry.is_null() {
